CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ lambda with class-reference parameter runs: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ lambda with by-value class parameter reads member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^(ERROR|error): member operator requires
--
N5008 [expr.prim.lambda.general]/4: a lambda parameter written with a concrete
class name is not a generic (auto) parameter.  CBMC replaced any cpp_name lambda
parameter with signed int, so accessing a member of a class-typed lambda
parameter failed and the enclosing body was dropped -- which stubbed
util/expr.cpp's exprt::visit to a no-op (a silent soundness loss).  assertion.3
FAILURE proves non-vacuity.
